<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>statistics-and-probability</title></head><body><h1>statistics-and-probability</h1><h2>Table of Contents</h2><ul><li>Measure of dispersion: standard deviation, variance, coef…</li><li>Probability: independent cases, mathematical and empirica…</li></ul><h2>Measure of dispersion: standard deviation, variance, coef…</h2><table><tr><th>#</th><th>Concept</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>**Scope.** Measure of dispersion: standard deviation, variance, coef… — Statistics and Probability, Mathematics (class-11-notes).</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>**Tested.** define it · list: measure of dispersion: standard deviation, variance, coefficient of variation, skewness · one worked example · one misconception each.</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>**Fact.** Dispersive power ω = (μv − μr)/(μd − 1); angular dispersion ΔD ∝ ω for a given refractive index.</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>**Fact.** Achromatism: net deviation of two cemented prisms is zero for a chosen colour → (ω₁/ω₂) relations on D/(μ−1).</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>**Fact.** Glass with higher Abbe number disperses less; flint glass > crown in dispersion.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>**Variance.** one-line definition + one-line exam use.</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>**Coefficient of variation.** one-line definition + one-line exam use.</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>**Skewness.** one-line definition + one-line exam use.</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>**Karl Pearson's coefficient of skewness.** one-line definition + one-line exam use.</td></tr></table><h3>Key Points</h3><table><tr><th>Point</th></tr><tr><td>• Measure of dispersion: standard deviation</td></tr><tr><td>• Variance</td></tr><tr><td>• Coefficient of variation</td></tr><tr><td>• Skewness</td></tr><tr><td>• Karl Pearson's coefficient of skewness</td></tr></table><h3>Common Confusions</h3><table><tr><th>❌ / ✅</th></tr><tr><td>❌ treat "Measure of dispersion: standard deviation" as one blob → ✅ split into: measure of dispersion: standard deviation, variance, coefficient of variation.</td></tr><tr><td>❌ state the rule without its limit → ✅ note when it applies / stops applying.</td></tr><tr><td>❌ answer with no steps → ✅ show each step and box the result.</td></tr><tr><td>❌ skip the key fact → ✅ dispersive power ω = (μv − μr)/(μd − 1); angular dispersion δd ∝ ω for a given refractive index..</td></tr></table><p><b>Summary:</b> Measure of dispersion: standard deviation, variance, coef… (Statistics and Probability, Mathematics, class-11-notes) covers Measure of dispersion: standard deviation, variance, coefficient of variation. Master the standard form, the sub-ideas and one worked example; most exam questions on this topic are built from exactly these.</p><hr><h2>Probability: independent cases, mathematical and empirica…</h2><table><tr><th>#</th><th>Concept</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>**Fact.** P(E) = favourable/total. Additive law: P(A∪B) = P(A)+P(B)−P(A∩B). If mutually exclusive, P(A∪B)=P(A)+P(B).</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>**Fact.** Multiplicative: P(A∩B) = P(A)P(B|A); independence: P(A∩B) = P(A)P(B).</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>**Fact.** Complement: P(A') = 1 − P(A). For discrete: ΣP = 1; expected value E(X) = Σxᵢpᵢ.</td></tr></table><h3>Key Points</h3><table><tr><th>Point</th></tr><tr><td>• Probability</td></tr><tr><td>• Independent cases</td></tr><tr><td>• Mathematical</td></tr><tr><td>• Empirical definition of probability</td></tr><tr><td>• Two basic laws of probability</td></tr><tr><td>• Without proof</td></tr><tr><td>Connection of Probability to other topics</td></tr><tr><td>Connection of Probability â€” Definitions and Basic Laws to other topics</td></tr></table><h3>Common Confusions</h3><table><tr><th>❌ / ✅</th></tr><tr><td>❌ answer with no steps → ✅ show each step and box the result.</td></tr><tr><td>❌ skip the key fact → ✅ p(e) = favourable/total. additive law: p(a∪b) = p(a)+p(b)−p(a∩b). if mutually exclusive, p(a∪b)=p(a)+p(b)..</td></tr></table><p><b>Summary:</b> Probability covers essential principles and applications. Probability â€” Definitions and Basic Laws covers essential principles and applications.</p><hr><h2>Comparison Tables</h2><h3>Concept Comparison</h3><table><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Description</th></tr><tr><td>1: Measure of dispersion: standard deviation, variance, coef…</td><td>Measure of dispersion: standard deviation, variance, coef… (Statistics and Probability, Mathematics, class-11-notes) covers Measure of dispersion: standard deviation, variance, coefficient of variation. Master the standard form, the sub-ideas and one worked example; most exam questions on this topic are built from exactly these.</td></tr><tr><td>2: Probability: independent cases, mathematical and empirica…</td><td>Probability covers essential principles and applications. Probability â€” Definitions and Basic Laws covers essential principles and applications.</td></tr></table></body></html>